!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/resolver-sidecar.tn"
!!meta:"https://tson.io/2026/32/m/meta.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/32/m/core.tn"
@doc:"""
  Formal shape of a resolver-layer sidecar (tests/resolver/**/*-expected.tn) -- see README.md's own
  "Valid resolver-layer vectors" section for the worked example this schema formalizes.
  Identification only (§4.3): base_value/number_form describe which of the four number-grammar
  forms a number matched and its own components, never a bound host numeric type.

  resolver_outcome is deliberately a single-member enum (valid) -- base type resolution (§4) never
  rejects a token, it always resolves to *something* (worst case, string), so no real vector, and
  therefore no field in this schema, needs an error/category shape at this layer.
  """
{
  @doc:"Fields every layer's sidecar shares -- spec/description are always present, encoding only when the .tn file isn't plain UTF-8."
  sidecar_common => {
    spec: text
    description: text
    encoding: text?
  }

  resolver_outcome => !enum [valid]

  base_value_kind => !enum [null boolean string number]
  number_form_shape => !enum [integer based-integer float special-value]
  number_form_sign => !enum [plus minus]
  number_form_radix => !enum [hex octal binary]
  number_form_special_kind => !enum [nan infinity]

  exponent => {
    sign: number_form_sign?
    digits: text
  }

  @doc:"""
    One of the four §7.6 number-grammar forms, discriminated by shape, every other field OPTIONAL
    and populated only for the shapes that actually carry it: integer needs sign/digits;
    based-integer needs sign/radix/digits; float needs sign/integer-part/fraction-digits/exponent;
    special-value needs sign/kind.
    """
  number_form => {
    shape: number_form_shape
    sign: number_form_sign?
    digits: text?
    radix: number_form_radix?
    integer-part: text?
    fraction-digits: text?
    exponent: exponent?
    kind: number_form_special_kind?
  }

  @doc:"""
    The result of base type resolution (§4), discriminated by kind. null/boolean carry a plain
    value; string carries its own text; number carries a full number_form.
    """
  base_value => {
    kind: base_value_kind
    value: text?
    text: text?
    form: number_form?
  }

  resolver_sidecar => sidecar_common & {
    outcome: resolver_outcome
    base-value: base_value?
  }
}
